exports[`review end to end > inline comments anchor to the reported line and only offer an apply that still fits 1`] = `
[
  {
    "body": "**HIGH bug:** Discount is multiplied by a hundred

applyDiscount multiplies the discounted total by 100, so every caller receives a total a hundred times too large.

- **Why this holds:** The added return statement multiplies the discounted total by a hundred.
- **Based on:** citation at \`src/pricing.ts:6\`; model-rationale at \`src/pricing.ts:6\`

Suggested fix: Return the discounted total without the stray factor of a hundred.

Finding: find_4945c4f21fdda7b2b02453ec

\`\`\`suggestion
  return order.total * factor
\`\`\`

<!-- codereviewer:finding:<fingerprint> -->",
    "line": 6,
    "path": "src/pricing.ts",
  },
  {
    "body": "**HIGH bug:** A negative percent is accepted

Nothing rejects a negative percent, so a negative discount raises the order total.

- **Why this holds:** No guard rejects a negative percent.
- **Based on:** citation at \`src/pricing.ts:5\`; model-rationale at \`src/pricing.ts:5\`

Suggested fix: Reject a percent outside 0..100 before computing the factor.

A concrete replacement was computed for this finding but does not have the shape a review comment can carry — it spans lines other than this comment's, or is more than one edit — so it is not offered as a one-click apply and was not checked against the file. It is recorded in full in \`report.json\` under this finding's \`fixProposal.edits\`.

Finding: find_f6346826ca25577a0a8cf727

<!-- codereviewer:finding:<fingerprint> -->",
    "line": 5,
    "path": "src/pricing.ts",
  },
]
