  - Check active-refutation: passed - The refuter was asked to disprove this candidate using only the code, diff ranges, and evidence it was shown. The verdict and its reasoning are recorded above. (evidence: ev_93d6de76ab1f362b73df908c, ev_876300865b8a47596fda53a5)
- Evidence this rests on:
  - citation at \`src/pricing.ts:5\`: // BUG: negative percents are not rejected
  - model-rationale at \`src/pricing.ts:5\`: No guard rejects a negative percent.
- Suggested fix (never applied automatically): Reject a percent outside 0..100 before computing the factor.
- Fix evidence: ev_93d6de76ab1f362b73df908c, ev_876300865b8a47596fda53a5
- Fix edits:
  - \`src/pricing.ts:5-6\`: \`if (percent < 0 || percent > 100) throw new RangeError("percent") return order.total * factor\`

Nothing rejects a negative percent, so a negative discount raises the order total.

### HIGH: Discount is multiplied by a hundred

- **This finding is why the quality gate failed.**
- Location: \`src/pricing.ts:6\` (file side)
